# Hermes Kanban — Command Reference

## States

| State | Meaning | How Cards Get There |
|-------|---------|---------------------|
| `todo` | Created but not yet ready to start | `kanban create` puts cards here |
| `ready` | Ready for the assigned profile to pick up | `kanban transition <id> ready` |
| `doing` | Currently being worked on by the assignee | `kanban transition <id> doing` (or auto by dispatcher) |
| `blocked` | Stuck, waiting on external input | `kanban block <id> "reason"` |
| `done` | Completed | `kanban complete <id>` |

The dispatcher automatically picks `ready` cards and transitions them to `doing`.

## Commands

### `hermes kanban create <title> [--assign <profile>] [--tag <tag>] [--parent <id>]`
Create a new card in `todo` state. The only required argument is the title.

- `--assign default` — handled by the main agent (no special profile needed)
- `--assign mike` — assigned to the `mike` profile
- `--tag study` — optional label for filtering
- `--parent t_xxx` — makes this card wait for another card to complete first
- `--body "text"` — detailed description

### `hermes kanban list [--tag <tag>] [--assignee <profile>] [--state <state>]`
View all cards. No arguments = everything. Can filter by tag, assignee, or state.

### `hermes kanban show <id>`
Full card details including body, comments, and run history.

### `hermes kanban transition <id> <state>`
Manually move a card between states: `todo → ready`, `ready → doing`, `doing → todo` (push back).

### `hermes kanban complete <id> [--summary "text"]`
Mark a card done. Optional summary.

### `hermes kanban block <id> "reason"`
Stick a card in `blocked`. The reason appears in notifications so the human or upstream knows what's needed.

### `hermes kanban unblock <id>`
Return a blocked card to `doing`.

### `hermes kanban comment <id> --body "text"`
Add a comment to a card's thread (doesn't change state).

### `hermes kanban tail <id>`
Live-stream the run log of an active card. Useful for watching a profile work.

## Filters and Views

```bash
# Filter by state
hermes kanban list --state ready

# Filter by tag
hermes kanban list --tag study

# Filter by assignee
hermes kanban list --assignee mike

# Combined
hermes kanban list --state doing --tag trade
```

## Common Workflow Patterns

### Solo (one profile, no extra setup)
```bash
hermes kanban create "Write Ames test draft" --assign default
hermes kanban transition t_abc123 ready
hermes kanban transition t_abc123 doing
# ... work happens ...
hermes kanban complete t_abc123
```

### Parallel research (fan-out)
```bash
hermes kanban create "Research A" --assign researcher
hermes kanban create "Research B" --assign researcher
hermes kanban create "Synthesize findings" --assign writer --parent t_a1 --parent t_b2
```
The synthesis card auto-promotes to `ready` only after both research cards complete.

### Pipeline with human review
```bash
hermes kanban create "Draft chapter" --assign writer
# Writer completes → human reviews → if changes needed:
hermes kanban create "Revise chapter" --assign writer --parent t_xxx
```

### Human-in-the-loop (blocking)
```bash
hermes kanban block t_xxx "Rate limit key: IP (NAT-unsafe) or user_id (requires auth)?"
# Human unblocks when decision is made
hermes kanban unblock t_xxx
```
